Agents in this directory vendored from affaan-m/ecc (MIT), 2026-09-14.

Chosen to match the stack this harness is used on — FastAPI, PostgreSQL +
pgvector, TypeScript/React — because a generic reviewer catches generic bugs:

  fastapi-reviewer       async correctness, DI, Pydantic schemas, OpenAPI
  database-reviewer      query plans, indexes, RLS, migration safety
  typescript-reviewer    type soundness, strict-mode gaps
  react-reviewer         render correctness, effect misuse
  rag-pipeline-reviewer  retrieval + embedding pipeline review
  tdd-guide              red/green/refactor discipline

Already present before this date, byte-identical to their ECC originals and
previously uncredited — this file corrects that attribution:

  code-reviewer          silent-failure-hunter  opensource-sanitizer

python-reviewer shares a name with ECC's but has diverged. Compared 2026-09-14:
the reviewer content is identical. The only differences are a `tools:` frontmatter
format nit and ECC's 9-line "Prompt Defense Baseline" — prose asking the agent to
treat fetched and third-party content as untrusted.

Deliberately NOT resynced. That concern is now enforced mechanically by
hooks/scripts/read-injection-scanner.js, which scans what Read, WebFetch and
WebSearch actually return and labels it as data. Per this repo's governing rule a
script that enforces beats prose that advises, and the prose costs ~1,100
characters on every invocation of every agent carrying it.

Note the resulting inconsistency, left visible on purpose: the six agents above
still carry the Baseline as vendored. Stripping it would mean editing six
upstream files and inviting merge pain on the next re-pin, for prose that is
harmless where it already sits. Do not ADD it to any new agent.
